<comment datatype='string'>The ring 1,2-phenylacetyl-CoA epoxidase, comprised of the PaaA, PaaB, PaaC, and PaaE polypeptides, catalyzes the second step in the aerobic degradation of phenylacetate [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21247899&quot;&gt;Grishin11&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
Stable subcomplexes composed of PaaABC, PaaAC and PaaBC can be purified, but only the combination of the PaaABC complex together with PaaE has full activity [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21247899&quot;&gt;Grishin11&lt;/a&gt;].  Crystal structures of the PaaAC subcomplex alone and together with a variety of ligands have been solved [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20823522&quot;&gt;Grishin10&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21247899&quot;&gt;Grishin11&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
